.TH NEO-DOCK 8 "2026-11-10" "gnome-phone 0.1.0" "GNOME Phone"
.SH NAME
neo-dock \- switch between the phone session and the GNOME desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neo-dock
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run on a display plug or unplug (by the opt-in udev rule /usr/share/gnome-phone-session/71-neo-dock.rules) and once at boot: with an external display connected it starts gnome-desktop.service, otherwise gnome-phone.service. Each executable in /etc/neo-dock.d/ is run first with "connected" or "disconnected". The file /run/neo-dock.off turns it off.
.SH SEE ALSO
systemctl(1)
